### Packages

{{ CAPITALIZED_CLI_NAME }} are organized into **packages** — collections of one or more {{ CLI_NAME }} that
can be created locally and optionally moved to a global location (`~/.{{ CLI_NAME }}/`)
for sharing across projects.
 has a `package.json` with a `{{ CLI_NAME }}` property mapping {{ SINGULAR_NAME }} names
  to their `instructions.json` paths.
- The project config at `{{ MAIN_FOLDER }}/config.json` lists installed packages in
  its `packages` array. Only {{ CLI_NAME }} from packages listed in the config are visible
  to `find` and `use` (config acts as a gatekeeper).
- Local packages (in `{{ MAIN_FOLDER }}/{{ INTERNAL_FOLDER }}/`) are prioritized over
  global packages (in `~/.{{ CLI_NAME }}/{{ INTERNAL_FOLDER }}/`) when resolving a
  {{ SINGULAR_NAME }} by name.
- To create a new package: `{{ CLI_CMD }} pack create <package-name>`
- To move a local package to global: `{{ CLI_CMD }} pack move <package-name> global`

### Multi-use vs Single-use

- **Multi-use {{ CLI_NAME }}** are recurring patterns you add multiple times with different
  variables (e.g., new API route, new view component). They keep structure
  consistent across repeated additions.
- **Single-use {{ CLI_NAME }}** are one-time additions to a project (e.g., add tailwind + shadcn,
  set up auth). You use them once. They can take variables (e.g., a project
  name or framework choice).

### Skills

This project scaffolds three skills:

| Skill | When to use |
|-------|-------------|
| `{{ CLI_NAME }}-brainstorm` | Planning new work — finds existing {{ CLI_NAME }}, classifies work, produces a plan document |
| `{{ CLI_NAME }}-implement` | Executing a plan document — works through tasks, finds/uses inline, invokes capture when needed |
